  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#48858\", \"PowerToys#47430\"], \"answer\": \"This is a known bug: the Command Palette Dock does not persist the network adapter chosen via 'Next Network', so after a restart it reverts to a different adapter (often the unused Ethernet one) and shows zeros. No permanent fix is described in the past tickets. Workarounds reported: disable the unused wired adapter, which one user said avoided the problem (#48858), or after each reboot re-select the correct network in the stats flyout (click the network item). Toggling the dock off and on in CmdPal settings can also help, though one user reported the selection still did not persist after that, so it may not be reliable (#47430). Add your details and bug report to #48858 so the team can track it.\"}",
